Second CI blocker found and fixed: VALIDATOR-CHECK's CSP Governance Gate
(exit 50, job "validate-pr") rejected this PR on `orb-widget.js` for
patterns that were 100% pre-existing on `origin/main`, unrelated to this
PR's diff:

$ git show origin/main:services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js > /tmp/orb-widget-main.js
$ python3 -c "<scan the 7 old CSP patterns against /tmp/orb-widget-main.js>"
script: 2 matches (both inside the top-of-file doc comment, e.g. L9, L56)
style_attr: 1 match (L345: `var style = document.createElement('style');`
  — a JS variable named "style", not an HTML style attribute)
dot_style: 26 matches (e.g. L3369, L3374: `.style.cssText = '...'` — normal
  DOM styling, not a CSP-relevant inline-style attribute set)
eval: 0, new_function: 0, unsafe_inline: 0
cdn: 1 match (L6, doc comment: `<script src="https://.../orb-widget.js">`)

This means the gate was unsatisfiable for ANY PR touching this file — a
governance regression, not a signal about this PR's content specifically.

Fix (this repo's own established pattern per VTID-03696/VTID-03505/03549 —
move fragile inline CI logic into the tested `.cjs` module rather than
patch it in place): added `cspFindings()` + `stripJsComments()` to
`scripts/ci/validator-path-guard.cjs`, wired via a new `--csp-scan` CLI
mode; `VALIDATOR-CHECK.yml`'s CSP step now calls that instead of the old
inline bash+python heredoc.

